     1,
     "<div>Dear group,</div><div> </div><div>I have been using this code of kohske&#39;s to align ggplot2 axes using grid:</div><div> </div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/7410525/align-ggplot2-axes-using-grid\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/7410525/align-ggplot2-axes-using-grid&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372894680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw258Ej10UuXKocjZmLtTUR-\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/7410525/align-ggplot2-axes-using-grid</a></div><div> </div><div>However, we had a UNIX/R update at work and now the code is not working.  The R version we are now using is 2.15.2 with ggplot2_0.9.3.</div><div> </div><div>The part of the code that is not working is replacing the removed panel.  I re-ran Kohske&#39;s code but replaced </div><div>grid<span>.</span><span>remove</span><span>(</span><span>&quot;panel-14-5&quot;</span><span>)</span><span>\r\n</span></div><div><span>with</span></div><div><span>grid.remove(&quot;panel-8.16-7-16-7&quot;)</span></div><div><span>which I determined using</span></div><div><span>sapply(grid.gget(^panel-&quot;,grep=TRUE),&quot;[[&quot;,&quot;name&quot;).</span></div><div><span></span> </div><div><span>However, when I try to replace </span></div><div><span><div>downViewport<span>(</span><span>&quot;panel-14-5&quot;</span><span>)</span></div><div><span>with</span></div><div><span>downViewport((&quot;panel-8.16-7-16-7&quot;)</span></div><div><span>I get the error </span></div><div><span>Error in grid.Call.graphics(L_downviewport, name$name, strict):</span></div><div><span>Viewport &#39;panel-8.16-7-16-7&#39; was not found.</span></div><div><span></span> </div><div><span>Any suggestions on how I can successful replace the removed panel would be greatly appreciated.</span></div><div><span></span> </div><div><span>Thank you so much for your help.</span></div><div><span></span> </div><div><span>Kim</span></div></span></div>"
    ]
